{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"The function separates multiple groups of nested parentheses into individual, balanced, non-nested strings.\n    It ignores spaces in the input string.\"\"\"\n    cleaned_string = paren_string.replace(\" \", \"\")\n\n    result_list: List[str] = []\n    balance = 0\n    current_group_start = None\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(cleaned_string):\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n\n        # Detect the start of a new top-level group\n        if balance == 1 and current_group_start is None:\n            current_group_start = i\n\n        # Detect the end of a top-level group\n        if balance == 0 and current_group_start is not None:\n            group = cleaned_string[current_group_start : i + 1]\n            result_list.append(group)\n            current_group_start = None\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/4", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef mean_absolute_deviation(numbers: List[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Mean Absolute Deviation (MAD) for a list of floating-point numbers.\n    It returns 0.0 if the input list is empty, as per design.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0.0\n\n    # Compute the mean of the numbers\n    mean_val = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\n\n    # Compute the absolute differences from the mean\n    absolute_differences = [abs(number - mean_val) for number in numbers]\n\n    # Compute the average of these absolute differences\n    mad_value = sum(absolute_differences) / len(absolute_differences)\n\n    return mad_value"}
