{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef _calculate_deepest_nesting_for_group(group_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the deepest level of nesting for a single group of parentheses.\n    It tracks the current and maximum nesting levels by iterating through characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max = 0\n    current_level = 0\n    for char in group_string:\n        if char == '(':\n            current_level += 1\n            current_max = max(current_max, current_level)\n        elif char == ')':\n            current_level -= 1\n    return current_max\n\n\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Input to this function is a string represented multiple groups for nested parentheses separated by spaces.\n    For each of the group, output the deepest level of nesting of parentheses.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    groups = paren_string.split(' ')\n    for group in groups:\n        nesting_level = _calculate_deepest_nesting_for_group(group)\n        results.append(nesting_level)\n    return results\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\nclass DepthCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Manages state and logic for calculating max nesting depth for a single group.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._current_depth = 0\n        self._max_depth = 0\n\n    def process_char(self, char: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Processes a single character to update current and maximum depths.\"\"\"\n        if char == '(':\n            self._current_depth += 1\n            if self._current_depth > self._max_depth:\n                self._max_depth = self._current_depth\n        elif char == ')':\n            self._current_depth -= 1\n\n    def get_max_depth(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the deepest nesting level encountered.\"\"\"\n        return self._max_depth\n\n\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Input to this function is a string represented multiple groups for nested parentheses separated by spaces.\n    For each of the group, output the deepest level of nesting of parentheses.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_depths = []\n    groups = paren_string.split(' ')\n\n    for group in groups:\n        calculator = DepthCalculator()\n        for char in group:\n            calculator.process_char(char)\n        max_depths.append(calculator.get_max_depth())\n\n    return max_depths\n```"}
