{"task_id": "HumanEval/25", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef factorize(n: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of prime factors for a given integer, ordered from smallest to largest, including multiplicity.\"\"\"\n    factors = []\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        factors.append(2)\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Handle odd factors starting from 3 up to the square root of n\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            factors.append(i)\n            n //= i\n        i += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 2, it must be a prime factor itself\n    if n > 2:\n        factors.append(n)\n\n    return factors"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n.\n    Returns 0 if n is less than or equal to 1, as no proper divisor exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 0\n\n    # Iterate downwards from n // 2 to 1 to find the largest proper divisor.\n    for i in range(n // 2, 0, -1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return i\n```"}
