{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "def find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs are coefficients of a polynomial.\n    find_zero find x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    find_zero returns only only zero point, even if there are many.\n    Moreover, find_zero only takes list xs having even number of coefficients\n    and largest non zero coefficient as it guarantees\n    a solution.\n    >>> round(find_zero([1, 2]), 2) # f(x) = 1 + 2x\n    -0.5\n    >>> round(find_zero([-6, 11, -6, 1]), 2) # (x - 1) * (x - 2) * (x - 3) = -6 + 11x - 6x^2 + x^3\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    low = -100.0\n    high = 100.0\n    max_iterations = 1000\n    tolerance = 1e-7\n\n    # Bisection method\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        mid = (low + high) / 2.0\n\n        val_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n        if abs(val_mid) < tolerance:\n            return mid\n\n        val_low = poly(xs, low)\n\n        # Check if root is in the left half [low, mid]\n        if val_low * val_mid < 0:\n            high = mid\n        # Check if root is in the right half [mid, high]\n        else:\n            low = mid\n\n    # If max_iterations reached without finding a zero within tolerance,\n    # return the midpoint of the final interval\n    return (low + high) / 2.0"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    return xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[1] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs are coefficients of a polynomial.\n    find_zero find x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    find_zero returns only only zero point, even if there are many.\n    Moreover, find_zero only takes list xs having even number of coefficients\n    and largest non zero coefficient as it guarantees\n    a solution.\n    >>> round(find_zero([1, 2]), 2) # f(x) = 1 + 2x\n    -0.5\n    >>> round(find_zero([-6, 11, -6, 1]), 2) # (x - 1) * (x - 2) * (x - 3) = -6 + 11x - 6x^2 + x^3\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(xs) % 2 != 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"The list of coefficients must have an even number of elements.\")\n    if not xs or xs[-1] == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"The largest coefficient (last element) must be non-zero.\")\n\n    # Handle the linear case directly for precision and efficiency\n    if len(xs) == 2:\n        return -xs[0] / xs[1]\n\n    tolerance = 1e-7\n    max_iterations = 100\n\n    # Check if 0 is a root.\n    if abs(poly(xs, 0.0)) < tolerance:\n        return 0.0\n\n    # Bisection method for root finding.\n    # We choose a sufficiently wide initial search range.\n    low, high = -100.0, 100.0\n\n    # Ensure initial interval has a sign change.\n    # For odd-degree polynomials with non-zero leading coefficient, this is guaranteed\n    # for a sufficiently large interval.\n    # If not, expand the interval until a sign change is found.\n    # For robust handling, we can expand the interval.\n    # The problem implies that a solution is guaranteed within reasonable bounds.\n    initial_search_limit = 10\n    current_low, current_high = low, high\n    for _ in range(initial_search_limit):\n        if (poly(xs, current_low) * poly(xs, current_high)) < 0:\n            low, high = current_low, current_high\n            break\n        current_low *= 2\n        current_high *= 2\n    else: # If no sign change found within the limit, use the expanded range.\n        low, high = -1000.0, 1000.0 # Fallback to a very wide range\n\n\n    # Main bisection loop\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        mid = (low + high) / 2\n        val_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n        if abs(val_mid) < tolerance:\n            return mid\n\n        val_low = poly(xs, low) # Re-evaluate to avoid propagating old val_low from previous iterations if low changed\n\n        if (val_low < 0 and val_mid > 0) or (val_low > 0 and val_mid < 0):\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            low = mid\n\n    # If max_iterations is reached, return the midpoint of the final interval.\n    return (low + high) / 2\n```\n"}
