{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively using memoization.\n    It handles base cases for n=0, 1, 2, 3 and applies the sum rule for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input Validation: Handle negative input\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input n must be non-negative\")\n\n    # Initialize memoization list with the first four base case values.\n    memo = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # If n is one of the base cases, return the pre-defined value directly.\n    if n < len(memo):\n        return memo[n]\n\n    # Iteratively calculate Fib4 values from the 4th element up to n.\n    for i in range(len(memo), n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = memo[i-1] + memo[i-2] + memo[i-3] + memo[i-4]\n        memo.append(next_fib4)\n\n    # Return the n-th Fib4 number from the memoization list.\n    return memo[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    Sorts the list and calculates the median based on its length.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    l.sort()\n    n = len(l)\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        mid1 = l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```"}
