{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    Sorts the list and finds the middle element or average of two middle elements.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3.0\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty for median calculation.\")\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For odd length, return the middle element.\n        return float(sorted_l[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # For even length, return the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\ndef modp(n: int, p: int):\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using modular exponentiation.\n    This handles large n efficiently and prevents overflow.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = 1\n    base = 2 % p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            result = (result * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        n //= 2\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes as input a string encoded with a shift function. Returns the decoded string\n    by shifting each character backward by 5 positions, handling alphabet wrapping.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char_code in s:\n        original_pos = ord(char_code) - ord('a')\n        # Shift backward by 5, ensuring positive result with +26 before modulo\n        shifted_pos = (original_pos - 5 + 26) % 26\n        new_char = chr(shifted_pos + ord('a'))\n        decoded_chars.append(new_char)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
