{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\ndef fibfib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the n-th element of the FibFib number sequence efficiently.\n    This implementation uses an iterative dynamic programming approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize the first three FibFib numbers\n    # fib0 = fibfib(n-3)\n    # fib1 = fibfib(n-2)\n    # fib2 = fibfib(n-1)\n    fib0, fib1, fib2 = 0, 0, 1\n\n    # Iteratively compute FibFib numbers up to n\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib0 + fib1 + fib2\n        fib0 = fib1\n        fib1 = fib2\n        fib2 = next_fib\n\n    return fib2\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\n# Module-level memoization cache for fibfib numbers.\n_memo: dict[int, int] = {}\n\ndef fibfib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the fibfib number sequence.\n    This function uses memoization for efficient calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_digits_string(x: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts an integer to its string representation.\"\"\"\n    return str(x)\n\ndef _get_number_of_digits(x: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of digits in an integer.\"\"\"\n    return len(str(x))\n\ndef _reverse_digits(digits_str: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the characters in a digit string.\"\"\"\n    return digits_str[::-1]\n\ndef _perform_right_shift(digits_str: str, shift_amount: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Performs a circular right shift on a digit string.\"\"\"\n    num_digits = len(digits_str)\n    effective_shift = shift_amount % num_digits\n    return digits_str[num_digits - effective_shift:] + digits_str[:num_digits - effective_shift]\n\ndef circular_shift(x: int, shift: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shifting digits right by shift.\n    If shift exceeds the number of digits, the digits are reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    digits_str = _get_digits_string(x)\n    num_digits = _get_number_of_digits(x)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        return _reverse_digits(digits_str)\n    else:\n        return _perform_right_shift(digits_str, shift)\n```\n"}
