{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "def closest_integer(value: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the closest integer to a number string, rounding away from zero if equidistant.\n    This custom rounding handles cases like 14.5 becoming 15 and -14.5 becoming -15.\n    \"\"\"\n    num = float(value)\n    fractional_part = abs(num - int(num))\n\n    if fractional_part == 0.5:\n        if num >= 0:\n            return int(num) + 1\n        else:\n            return int(num) - 1\n    else:\n        return round(num)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/100", "solution": "```python\ndef make_a_pile(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, you have to make a pile of n levels of stones.\n    The first level has n stones.\n    The number of stones in the next level is:\n        - the next odd number if n is odd.\n        - the next even number if n is even.\n    Return the number of stones in each level in a list, where element at index\n    i represents the number of stones in the level (i+1).\n\n    Examples:\n    >>> make_a_pile(3)\n    [3, 5, 7]\n    \"\"\"\n    stone_counts = []\n    stone_counts.append(n)\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        previous_stones = stone_counts[i-1]\n        current_stones = previous_stones + 2\n        stone_counts.append(current_stones)\n\n    return stone_counts\n```"}
