{"task_id": "HumanEval/137", "solution": "```python\nclass RealNumberRepresentation:\n    \"\"\"\n    Encapsulates a real number, storing its original representation and a float for comparison.\n    Handles various input types and decimal separators during parsing.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self._original_value = value\n        self._numeric_value = self._parse_real_number(value)\n\n    def _parse_real_number(self, value) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Converts the input value to a float, handling string representations with commas.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Convert to string, replace comma, then convert to float.\n        # This handles int, float, and string inputs uniformly.\n        return float(str(value).replace(',', '.'))\n\n    def get_original_value(self):\n        \"\"\"Returns the value as it was originally passed.\"\"\"\n        return self._original_value\n\n    def get_numeric_value(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Returns the parsed numeric (float) value for comparison.\"\"\"\n        return self._numeric_value\n\ndef compare_one(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Create a function that takes integers, floats, or strings representing\n    real numbers, and returns the larger variable in its given variable type.\n    Return None if the values are equal.\n    Note: If a real number is represented as a string, the floating point might be . or ,\n\n    compare_one(1, 2.5) \u279e 2.5\n    compare_one(1, \"2,3\") \u279e \"2,3\"\n    compare_one(\"5,1\", \"6\") \u279e \"6\"\n    compare_one(\"1\", 1) \u279e None\n    \"\"\"\n    num_a = RealNumberRepresentation(a)\n    num_b = RealNumberRepresentation(b)\n\n    a_num = num_a.get_numeric_value()\n    b_num = num_b.get_numeric_value()\n\n    if a_num > b_num:\n        return num_a.get_original_value()\n    elif b_num > a_num:\n        return num_b.get_original_value()\n    else:\n        return None\n```"}
