{"task_id": "HumanEval/158", "solution": "```python\ndef _count_unique_characters(s):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of unique characters in a string.\"\"\"\n    return len(set(s))\n\ndef find_max(words):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the word with the maximum unique characters from a list of strings.\n    Applies lexicographical tie-breaking for words with equal unique character counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not words:\n        return \"\"\n\n    max_unique_count = -1\n    result_string = \"\"\n\n    for current_string in words:\n        unique_count = _count_unique_characters(current_string)\n\n        if unique_count > max_unique_count:\n            max_unique_count = unique_count\n            result_string = current_string\n        elif unique_count == max_unique_count:\n            # For ties, choose the lexicographically smaller string.\n            if current_string < result_string:\n                result_string = current_string\n\n    return result_string\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/159", "solution": "```python\ndef eat(number: int, need: int, remaining: int) -> list[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates total carrots eaten and remaining stock after a meal.\n    If insufficient carrots are available, all remaining carrots are consumed.\"\"\"\n\n    if remaining >= need:\n        carrots_consumed = need\n        carrots_left = remaining - need\n    else:  # remaining < need\n        carrots_consumed = remaining\n        carrots_left = 0\n\n    total_eaten_carrots = number + carrots_consumed\n\n    return [total_eaten_carrots, carrots_left]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "```python\ndef do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs an algebraic expression from operators and operands, then evaluates it.\n    It returns the numerical result of the expression.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _construct_expression_string(ops, nums):\n        \"\"\"Interleaves numbers and operators to form an algebraic expression string.\"\"\"\n        expression_parts = []\n        for i in range(len(nums)):\n            expression_parts.append(str(nums[i]))\n            if i < len(ops):\n                expression_parts.append(ops[i])\n        return \"\".join(expression_parts)\n\n    def _evaluate_expression_string(expression_str):\n        \"\"\"Evaluates the given expression string using Python's built-in eval function.\"\"\"\n        return eval(expression_str)\n\n    # Note: Input validation (_validate_inputs) as per design is omitted\n    # due to critical requirements forbidding isinstance checks and error raising.\n\n    expression_string = _construct_expression_string(operator, operand)\n    result = _evaluate_expression_string(expression_string)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "```python\ndef do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs an algebraic expression by interleaving operands and operators, then evaluates it.\n    Uses Python's eval() for evaluation, respecting standard mathematical precedence.\n    \"\"\"\n    expression_parts = []\n    expression_parts.append(str(operand[0]))\n\n    for i in range(len(operator)):\n        expression_parts.append(operator[i])\n        expression_parts.append(str(operand[i + 1]))\n\n    expression_string = \" \".join(expression_parts)\n    return int(eval(expression_string))\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/162", "solution": "```python\nimport hashlib\nfrom typing import Optional\n\ndef string_to_md5(text: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string 'text', return its md5 hash equivalent string.\n    If 'text' is an empty string, return None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return None\n    else:\n        # Encode the string to bytes (UTF-8) and compute its MD5 hash.\n        md5_hash = hashlib.md5(text.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n        return md5_hash\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "```python\ndef solve(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Processes an input string based on specific character-processing rules.\n    If the string contains no letters, reverse the string; otherwise, reverse the case of alphabetic characters and keep others as is.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_alphabetic(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given character is an alphabetic letter (a-z, A-Z).\"\"\"\n        return 'a' <= char <= 'z' or 'A' <= char <= 'Z'\n\n    def _reverse_char_case(char: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Reverses the case of an alphabetic character; returns unchanged for non-alphabetic.\"\"\"\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            return char.upper()\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            return char.lower()\n        return char\n\n    def _has_letters(s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the input string contains at least one alphabetic letter.\"\"\"\n        for char in s:\n            if _is_alphabetic(char):\n                return True\n        return False\n\n    def _reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Reverses the order of characters in the entire input string.\"\"\"\n        return s[::-1]\n\n    if not _has_letters(s):\n        return _reverse_string(s)\n    else:\n        processed_chars = []\n        for char in s:\n            processed_chars.append(_reverse_char_case(char))\n        return \"\".join(processed_chars)\n\n```"}
