{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "```python\ndef solve(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms an input string by reversing letter cases and conditionally\n    reversing the entire string based on the presence of letters in the original input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    processed_chars = []\n    original_has_letters = False\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            original_has_letters = True\n            # Reverse case: lowercase to uppercase, uppercase to lowercase.\n            processed_chars.append(char.swapcase())\n        else:\n            # Keep non-letters as they are.\n            processed_chars.append(char)\n\n    result_string = \"\".join(processed_chars)\n\n    # If the original string contained no letters at all, reverse the entire resulted string.\n    if not original_has_letters:\n        return result_string[::-1]\n    else:\n        return result_string\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "```python\ndef generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two integers a and b, return a list of even single-digit numbers\n    between a and b (inclusive), in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine the lower and upper bounds from the input integers.\n    lower_bound = min(a, b)\n    upper_bound = max(a, b)\n\n    result = []  # Initialize an empty list for collecting results.\n    candidate_digits = [2, 4, 6, 8]  # Define the fixed list of candidate even single-digits.\n\n    # Iterate through candidate digits and append those within the specified range.\n    for digit in candidate_digits:\n        if lower_bound <= digit <= upper_bound:\n            result.append(digit)\n\n    # Ensure the final list is in ascending order as required by the design.\n    result.sort()\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "```python\ndef generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n\n    For example:\n    generate_integers(2, 8) => [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    generate_integers(8, 2) => [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    generate_integers(10, 14) => []\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_bound = min(a, b)\n    upper_bound = max(a, b)\n    result_list = []\n\n    # Iterate through possible single-digit even numbers\n    for num in [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]:\n        if lower_bound <= num <= upper_bound:\n            result_list.append(num)\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
